<section>
    <h1>About Mara Voss</h1>
    <p class="intro">
        Mara Voss is a fictional digital archivist and interactive media
        designer based in Port Alder, Oregon.
    </p>
    <p>
        She is especially interested in <strong>digital preservation</strong>,
        <em>interactive storytelling</em>, and accessible web design.
    </p>
    <p>
        Mara believes technology should help people understand historical
        materials without removing them from their original context.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
        Mara grew up in a coastal town where her mother worked at a local
        history museum and her father repaired old books.
    </p>
    <p>
        Her early exposure to photographs, letters, maps, and damaged books
        encouraged her to study how digital tools can preserve cultural memory.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <p>
        <strong>North Coast Institute of Design</strong><br>
        B.A. in Digital Media and Information Studies
    </p>
    <p>
        During college, Mara focused on archival research, information
        organization, and interactive media.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Professional Interests</h2>
    <ul>
